  "id": "yester_hill_gulthias_tree",
  "name": "The Crown of Yester Hill",
  "region": "yester_hill",
  "summary": "The top of Yester Hill inside a ring of standing stones: a black, twisted tree that drinks what it is given, a fire, and a great earthen effigy of the lord of the valley, lying on its back with a stone in its heart.",
  "text": "The crown of the hill is flat and bare inside its ring of stones. In the middle stands a tree with bark like a burnt hand and roots that go into the ground the way fingers go into a wound. Beside it lies a man made of earth and timber, forty feet long, cloaked, with a face you have seen before.",
